.TH COF-UNTRUST 1 "2026-11-13" "cof 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cof-untrust \- Stop applying a project config file you trusted
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
cof untrust [OPTIONS] [path]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes a project config file from ~/.config/circuitry/trusted.json, so it is
no longer applied automatically.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B PATH
Config file to untrust (default: circuitry.config.json or config.json in the
current directory).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cof untrust
Untrusts circuitry.config.json or config.json in the current directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/trusted.json
Where every trust decision is recorded.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed, or the input was invalid.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error -- an unrecognized option or missing argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcof(1)\fR, \fBcof-trust(1)\fR
